# Milestone: W4/v0.10.2 (updated v0.10.9-tag-state W2: D3 outside-scope fatal)
# Covers: Tag.new() constructor returns a UVAL_TAG; t.stop() called outside
#         any active scope for `t` escalates to fatal (D3 ratify); t.freeze()
#         / t.unfreeze() are callable and return nil.
# Activated: v0.10.2-reactive W4 (UVAL_TAG + Tag.new() + scripted .stop()).
#
# Note: the original M3 draft tested that t.stop() INSIDE a t: scope
# terminates execution (echo("before") prints; echo("after") does not).
# That semantics requires W5 (bare-prefix tag-label binding) so OP_PUSH_TAG
# uses the register's UVAL_TAG as the scope's owning tag.  At W4 baseline
# OP_PUSH_TAG creates an anonymous UTag independent of `t`; calling t.stop()
# stops the `t` tag-member-list but the scope's anonymous tag continues.
#
# v0.10.9-tag-state W2: t.stop() outside any active scope for the receiver
# escalates to fatal (was silent nil pre-W2).  Workspace-root
# compatibility-decisions ledger §S5c.  Closes design-risks v0.10.7-D.
# Test now exercises both reachability AND the D3 outside-scope fatal path.

var t = Tag.new("sc")
t.stop()
var t2 = Tag.new("fr")
t2.freeze()
t2.unfreeze()
[00000000] <Tag: sc>
[00000001] !!! tag.stop with no active scope
[00000002] <Tag: fr>
[00000003] nil
[00000004] nil
